# Epoch build products: game and arc jars produced from the reference clones. They are large, they
# are reproducible with :prepareEpochVn, and they are not sources.
.mindustry/
.arc/

# Gradle build trees and caches, one per module plus this root: every one of them is reproducible
# and the jar alone is several megabytes. Covers core/build, pack/build and build/ alike, and
# native/build on top of native/.gitignore.
build/
.gradle/

# IDE state, which belongs to whoever opened the project. native/.clangd stays tracked: it names the
# ABI whose compile database indexes the sources and the diagnostics this project wants silenced,
# which is knowledge about the project rather than about one editor.
.idea/
.vscode/

# The SDK location, as the header of the file itself says.
local.properties

# Leftovers of running the bridge by hand from this directory. arc looks a library up as a classpath
# resource and, failing that, unpacks it into the working directory, so what it leaves behind is one
# libarc*.so per library it was handed - the infix is why the pattern is not the arm64 spelling,
# which is only what one device produced - and its own unpacking directory. Neither is a source, and
# both come back the next time someone tests a command line here.
libarc*.so
.temp/

# A JVM started by hand from here drops its crash report and its heap dump into the working
# directory: both are large, machine specific, and worthless to anyone else.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.hprof

# Editor and file manager droppings from the other platforms this is built on.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
